    "body": "## Summary\n\n**ADR-063 — Whitelist `float` + `clear`.** 2-line change unlocks ~180 lines of ADR-030/036 float layout.\n\n**Fixture-verified only.** Wikipedia visual verification blocked by separate scroll bug (ADR-064).\n\n## Verified delta (fixture)\n\n5-second fixture shows `float: right` working: orange box right-aligned, following text starts at left. Matches ADR-030's block-narrowing approximation exactly.\n\n## Not verified\n\nWikipedia visual delta — user cannot scroll (scrollbar missing). Deferred to ADR-064.\n\n## The change\n\nTwo strings added to `supported_properties()`:\n- `\"float\"`\n- `\"clear\"`\n\n## What this unlocks\n\n`layout.cpp:1205-1390` has complete ADR-030/036 implementation: float placement, `float_left_w`/`float_right_w`/`float_bottom` accumulation, block-child narrowing, `clear: left/right/both` jumps. **All dead code** before this whitelist add — `get(\"float\")` returned nullopt on every page.\n\n## Test count\n\n687 / 2627 unchanged (zero existing float tests).\n\n## Verification category\n\nFixture-verified. Production-visual deferred to scroll fix.\n\nRefs #267\n",
